\fs24
\b APB UART Micro-Architecture\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Overview\b0\par
This document describes the APB UART RTL architecture in apb_uart.sv. The design is a single APB slave UART block with integrated TX/RX FIFO memories and RTS/CTS flow control.\par
\par
\b 2. External Interface\b0\par
\b APB:\b0 pclk, presetn, psel, penable, pwrite, paddr[7:0], pwdata[31:0], prdata[31:0], pready, pslverr.\par
\b UART:\b0 uart_tx, uart_rx.\par
\b Flow control:\b0 cts_i (input), rts_o (output).\par
\b Interrupt:\b0 irq.\par
\par
\b 3. Register Map\b0\par
\b 0x00 DATA\b0\tab Write pushes pwdata[7:0] into TX FIFO. Read pops/returns RX FIFO byte.\par
\b 0x04 STATUS\b0\tab [0] tx_full, [1] tx_empty, [2] rx_full, [3] rx_empty, [4] cts_i, [5] rts_o, [15:8] tx_count, [23:16] rx_count.\par
\b 0x08 CTRL\b0\tab [0] uart_en, [1] tx_en, [2] rx_en, [3] irq_en.\par
\b 0x0C BAUD\b0\tab [15:0] baud_div (0 ignored).\par
\par
\b 4. Integrated FIFO Micro-Architecture\b0\par
The UART RTL includes internal FIFO memories (no standalone external FIFO module required):\par
- TX FIFO: tx_mem, tx_wptr, tx_rptr, tx_count.\par
- RX FIFO: rx_mem, rx_wptr, rx_rptr, rx_count.\par
Both FIFOs support push, pop, and simultaneous push+pop operations.\par
\par
\b 5. UART TX Datapath\b0\par
TX FSM states: TX_IDLE, TX_START, TX_DATA, TX_STOP.\par
Transmission starts only when: uart_en=1, tx_en=1, TX FIFO not empty, and cts_i=1.\par
Output format is 8N1.\par
\par
\b 6. UART RX Datapath\b0\par
RX FSM states: RX_IDLE, RX_START, RX_DATA, RX_STOP.\par
RX detects start bit, samples 8 data bits on baud ticks, checks stop bit, and pushes to RX FIFO if not full.\par
\par
\b 7. Flow Control\b0\par
- cts_i gates TX launch from TX_IDLE.\par
- rts_o indicates local receive readiness using RX FIFO occupancy threshold (rx_count < FIFO_DEPTH-2).\par
\par
\b 8. Clocking, Reset, Interrupt\b0\par
- presetn (active-low) resets registers, FIFO pointers/counts, and FSM state.\par
- Shared baud divider generates baud_tick for both TX/RX.\par
- irq = irq_en AND (!rx_empty OR rx_full OR tx_full).\par
}
